<!--
	widgets.xml - migrated from v2 overrides.xml <widget-groupings> (lines 78-268)

	MIGRATION NOTES (read before editing):
	- v2 <node label="X"> .................... -> v3 <group name="..." label="X">
	- v2 <shortcut ...>path</shortcut> ....... -> v3 <widget ...><path>path</path></widget>
	- v2 widget="KIND" (the widget kind) ..... -> v3 source="..." (output property: widgetSource)
	      library  -> library      tmdb -> addon       pvr -> pvr
	      addon    -> addon        favourites -> favourites
	      (.xsp playlists were widget="library" in v2; kept as source="library" to match
	       v2 artwork handling, which treats library and playlist identically)
	- v2 widgetType="..." ................... -> v3 type="..."   (output property: widgetType)
	- v2 widgetTarget="..." .................. -> v3 target="..." (output property: widgetTarget)
	- v2 condition="..." (Kodi runtime) ...... -> v3 visible="..." (runtime visibility)
	- v2 icon="..." .......................... -> v3 icon="..." (kept verbatim)
	- v2 label="123"/$ADDON[]/$LOCALIZE[] .... kept verbatim (skinshortcuts auto-localizes numeric IDs)

	WATCH-POINTS (preserved v2 values that fall outside the documented v3 enum; flagged, not changed):
	- target="pvr"   on Live TV / Radio channel + timer widgets (v2 used widgetTarget=pvr)
	- target="games" on the Games add-on widget       (v2 used widgetTarget=games)
	  -> If v3 rejects these, the documented equivalents are tv/radio and programs respectively.

	DEFERRED TO templates.xml PHASE (info-kind widgets whose v2 "path" is a $INCLUDE template,
	not a real content path). Marked inline below with "DEFERRED" comments so the picker
	structure is preserved. They re-enter once we decide the v3 template strategy:
	    Live TV   -> TVRecordings
	    Radio     -> RadioRecordings
	    Weather   -> WeatherContentDaily / WeatherContentHourly / (WeatherContent36Hour, was commented out)
	    System    -> SystemContent/CPU/Memory/Storage/Network/Uptime/Battery/Video/PVR/Version
	    Favourites-> CustomFavouriteContent / CustomFavouriteAddonContent
-->
